From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:05:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 029/207] server: carry the Spark stats wire for DeepSeek-V4.1
 responses

The published DeepSeek-V4.1 engine answers with the Spark server's
tensorfold block (prompt, cached, ttft_s, finish, completion, prefill_s,
decode_s, rounds, drafted, accepted), and the benchmark and smoke driver
reads those keys. Add them to the native block, after its own keys, when the
checkpoint's model_type is deepseek_v41 or deepseek_v4; TENSORFOLD_WIRE=spark
forces them on and native (or tensorfold) forces them off. Whole replies and
the final streamed chunk both carry them. Native keys and the speculative
object are unchanged, and other families' replies are byte-identical.

Test: spark_wire_test.zig serves a completion through openai.run with a
scripted engine, whole and streamed, and checks each Spark value and that
the block less those keys equals the native reply; spark_wire.zig tests the
TENSORFOLD_WIRE overrides.
